<title>USA: Fujitsu launches offer for Amdahl.</title>
<headline>Fujitsu launches offer for Amdahl.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fujitsu Ltd and Amdahl Corp Tuesday jointly announced Fujitsu's official launch of its $12.00 per share tender offer for all the outstanding common shares of Amdahl it does not already own.</p>
<p>Last week, Fujitsu announced it planned to acquire the shares. The deal is valued at a total $850 million. Fujitsu already owns 42 percent of Amdahl, a maker of IBM-compatible mainframe computers and related data storage systems. The transaction has been approved by Amdahl's board of directors.</p>
<p>The tender offer and withdrawal rights will expire at 1700 EDT, Friday, Sept. 5.</p>
